---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import ServiceCard from "../components/ServiceCard.astro";
import CTABanner from "../components/CTABanner.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../data/siteConfig";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@type": "Service",
    name: "Heating Services",
    serviceType: "Heating",
    description: "Complete Home Comfort provides expert heating solutions in Pittsburgh including furnace installation and repair, heat pump services, boiler maintenance, and ductless heating systems.",
    provider: { "@id": `${siteConfig.url}/#organization` },
    areaServed: { "@type": "City", name: "Pittsburgh", addressRegion: "PA" },
    url: `${siteConfig.url}/heating/`,
    hasOfferCatalog: {
      "@type": "OfferCatalog",
      name: "Heating Services",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "Offer", itemOffered: { "@type": "Service", name: "Furnace Installation & Repair" } },
        { "@type": "Offer", itemOffered: { "@type": "Service", name: "Heat Pump Services" } },
        { "@type": "Offer", itemOffered: { "@type": "Service", name: "Boiler Services" } },
        { "@type": "Offer", itemOffered: { "@type": "Service", name: "Ductless Heating" } },
      ],
    },
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Heating Services"
  description="Professional heating services in Pittsburgh - furnaces, heat pumps, boilers, and ductless heating. Call (412) 757-2301."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <PageHero
    title="Heating Services"
    subtitle="Keep your home warm and comfortable all winter long"
    bgClass="bg1"
  />

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="w-full max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 fade-in">
      <p>When Pittsburgh winters bring freezing temperatures and heavy snowfall, a reliable heating system is essential for your family's comfort and safety. At Complete Home Comfort, owner Ethan Bailey and our team are committed to providing quality heating solutions tailored to your home's unique needs. Whether you need a new furnace installed, a heat pump serviced, or an emergency boiler repair, we bring the expertise and dedication to get the job done right the first time.</p>
      <p>We work with homeowners throughout the Pittsburgh area to ensure their heating systems run efficiently all season long. From selecting the right equipment to professional installation and ongoing maintenance, we are here to help you stay warm without breaking the bank on energy costs.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-surface">
    <div class="w-full max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-12 fade-in">
        <span class="inline-block text-chc-blue font-semibold text-[0.85rem] uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Our Heating Solutions</span>
        <h2>Comprehensive Heating Services</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 fade-in">
        <ServiceCard icon="fas fa-fire" iconColor="red" title="Furnaces" description="We install, repair, and maintain both gas and electric furnaces from trusted manufacturers. Our team specializes in high-efficiency models that deliver consistent warmth throughout your home while helping reduce your monthly energy bills. Whether your existing furnace needs a tune-up or it's time for a full replacement, we will help you find the right solution." link={{ text: "Schedule Service", href: "/contact/" }} />
        <ServiceCard icon="fas fa-temperature-arrow-up" iconColor="red" title="Heat Pumps" description="Heat pumps offer an energy-efficient two-in-one solution for both heating and cooling your home. Using modern heat pump technology, these systems transfer heat rather than generate it, resulting in lower operating costs. We provide expert installation, repair, and maintenance for all heat pump brands and models." link={{ text: "Schedule Service", href: "/contact/" }} />
        <ServiceCard icon="fas fa-temperature-high" iconColor="red" title="Boilers" description="Boilers remain a popular and effective heating choice for many Pittsburgh homes, especially older properties with radiator or radiant floor systems. We service both hot water and steam boilers, providing installation, routine maintenance, and repair to keep your system running safely and efficiently throughout the heating season." link={{ text: "Schedule Service", href: "/contact/" }} />
        <ServiceCard icon="fas fa-wind" iconColor="red" title="Ductless Heating" description="Ductless mini-split systems provide targeted zone heating without the need for ductwork, making them an ideal choice for home additions, converted garages, sunrooms, and older homes that lack existing duct systems. These units are quiet, energy-efficient, and allow you to control the temperature in individual rooms." link={{ text: "Schedule Service", href: "/contact/" }} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="w-full max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 fade-in">
      <div class="text-center mb-8">
        <h2>Should I Repair or Replace My Heating System?</h2>
      </div>
      <p>One of the most common questions homeowners face is whether to repair their current heating system or invest in a new one. The answer depends on several factors, including the age of your equipment, the frequency of repairs, and your energy costs. Here are some guidelines to help you decide.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-8">
        <div class="bg-white border border-card-border rounded-xl p-8 shadow-card-sm">
          <h3>Consider Repair If</h3>
          <ul class="service-list">
            <li>Your system is less than 10 years old</li>
            <li>The issue is minor and isolated, such as a faulty thermostat or a clogged filter</li>
            <li>The cost of the repair is significantly less than the cost of replacement</li>
            <li>Your system has been well-maintained and has no history of recurring problems</li>
            <li>Your energy bills have remained steady over the past few years</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-card-border rounded-xl p-8 shadow-card-sm">
          <h3>Consider Replacement If</h3>
          <ul class="service-list">
            <li>Your system is 15 or more years old</li>
            <li>You are calling for repairs frequently, especially within the same season</li>
            <li>Your energy bills have been steadily rising despite regular maintenance</li>
            <li>Some rooms in your home are consistently too hot or too cold</li>
            <li>Your system uses an outdated or discontinued refrigerant</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8">Not sure which option is right for you? Contact us for a free consultation - we will give you our honest recommendation based on what makes the most sense for your home and budget.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-surface">
    <div class="w-full max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 fade-in">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto text-center">
        <h2>Proud Armstrong Air Dealer</h2>
        <p>As an authorized Armstrong Air dealer, Complete Home Comfort offers a full line of dependable, high-efficiency heating equipment backed by one of the most trusted names in the industry. Armstrong Air has been manufacturing quality HVAC systems since 1928, building a reputation for durable construction, quiet operation, and energy-saving performance.</p>
        <p>When you choose an Armstrong Air heating system, you benefit from advanced engineering, strong warranty protection, and the confidence that comes from nearly a century of manufacturing excellence. Combined with our professional installation and service, an Armstrong Air system is an investment in long-term home comfort.</p>
        <a href="https://www.armstrongair.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-outline mt-4">Learn More About Armstrong Air</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABanner
    title="Stay Warm This Winter"
    description="Whether you need a new heating system, a repair, or routine maintenance, our team is ready to help you stay comfortable all season long."
  />
</BaseLayout>
